or Eggleston, confirmed this with us a short while ago, and also the opposition wanted to seek a further extension of time. John Hogg Is it just part (b) that you are opposing, and not part (a)? Stephen Parry Yes. Without having the full details, I would imagine it would be just part (b). It is the COAG Reform Fund Bill 2008. Anne McEwen We are talking about the Economics Committee reports. Stephen Parry That is correct. John Hogg Senator McEwen, may I suggest that you split your motion. Those who are in favour of part (a) of the motion which relates to the North West Shelf project, say ‘aye’; to the contrary ‘no’. Anne McEwen Question agreed to. John Hogg I will now put the second part of the motion, which relates to the COAG Reform Fund Bill 2008. The question is that the motion in respect of paragraph (b) be agreed to.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1542","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2008-11-10/2"}
